# The system services of the Luna Linux desktop.
# The login screen. The unit conflicts with getty@tty1, which is intended:
# greetd takes over the first console instead of the usual login prompt.
enable greetd.service

# Power profiles. Without the daemon running, the panel control has nothing to
# talk to and the laptop stays on whatever the firmware chose.
enable power-profiles-daemon.service

# Bluetooth. bluez, its tools and blueman were all installed and the panel had
# a bluetooth button, while bluetoothd was never started by anything - so on a
# freshly installed system Bluetooth simply did not work.
#
# Safe to enable unconditionally. The unit carries
# ConditionPathIsDirectory=/sys/class/bluetooth, so on a machine with no
# adapter it is skipped rather than failed, and systemd's own udev rule
# (99-systemd.rules) pulls bluetooth.target in when an adapter appears. A
# desktop with no Bluetooth starts nothing; plug a dongle into it and the
# daemon comes up by itself.
enable bluetooth.service
